If an item is wrong, write a one-sentence error analysis: what went wrong and how you will fix it next time.

## Worked example

Garden 8 ft by 5 ft: area = 8 × 5 = 40 square feet; perimeter = 2(8+5) = 26 feet. Always label square feet vs feet.

## Watch for this mistake

A frequent error in **Area of Triangles and Polygons** is treating a slogan or a one-word label as mastery. Instead, restate the definition, show the worked example from memory, then complete practice with labeled steps or cited evidence.

## Practice

Complete these on your own first.

1. State one model you can draw for today''s skill.
2. Why label units on the final answer?
3. Name one check strategy after computing.

## Check your work

Compare your answers only after you finish.

1. Answers vary: array, number line, area model, tape diagram, etc., matched to the skill.
2. Units tell what the number measures and prevent mixing length with area/volume.
3. Estimate, inverse operation, or re-compute with a different method.

## Stretch

