## Watch for this mistake

A frequent error in **U.S. Civil Rights Milestones** is treating a slogan or a one-word label as mastery. Instead, restate the definition, show the worked example from memory, then complete practice with labeled steps or cited evidence.

## Practice

Complete these on your own first.

1. Purpose vs tone: which describes attitude?
2. Name one diction clue that a text may be trying to persuade.
3. Give one logos example and one pathos example you might find in an article.

