Science explains patterns with models. For Ecology and Biodiversity, name the key parts/processes and how they interact.

Consider edge cases and counterexamples. Strong reasoning means knowing both when a rule applies and when it does not.

### Core concept 2

Distinguish observation (what you see/measure) from inference (what you conclude). Controlled comparisons improve investigations.

Consider edge cases and counterexamples. Strong reasoning means knowing both when a rule applies and when it does not.

### Core concept 3

Link structure to function: why a part''s shape or arrangement enables what it does (cells, molecules, Earth systems, forces).

Consider edge cases and counterexamples. Strong reasoning means knowing both when a rule applies and when it does not.

