INSERT INTO "Lesson" VALUES('cmuh9bydi09vvedanothx8jrl','cmuh9bydh09vtedancw8rs5y1','Why Word Study Matters','Approach Scripture with reverence, careful reading, and attention to original words.','Welcome to **Bible: Hallelujah Scriptures & Paleo-Hebrew Word Study** at Prosper Preparatory (Grade 10).

Today''s lesson: **Why Word Study Matters**. Approach Scripture with reverence, careful reading, and attention to original words.

This course studies Scripture through the **Hallelujah Scriptures** framing, with careful attention to **Paleo-Hebrew letter forms**, **Hebrew roots**, and **original word meanings**. Work reverently and academically.

## Learning goals
- Hallelujah Scriptures emphasize the Name and a return to Hebraic understanding of the text.
- Word study slows reading so meaning is not skipped; roots and usage clarify English renderings.
- We study academically and faithfully — seeking understanding for obedience, not for arguments.

## Teach
### Study point 1

Hallelujah Scriptures emphasize the Name and a return to Hebraic understanding of the text.

In your notebook: record the term, a short gloss, and one contextual observation from the passage.
### Study point 2

Word study slows reading so meaning is not skipped; roots and usage clarify English renderings.

In your notebook: record the term, a short gloss, and one contextual observation from the passage.
### Study point 3

We study academically and faithfully — seeking understanding for obedience, not for arguments.

In your notebook: record the term, a short gloss, and one contextual observation from the passage.

## Word-study method (use every lesson)

1. **Read the passage** in your Hallelujah Scriptures text (teacher-provided edition).
2. **Select 1–2 key words** — verbs of action, covenant terms, names/titles, or praise vocabulary.
3. **Note the Hebrew root** (as available in class tools): consonants, basic glosses, and related forms.
4. **Check context**: surrounding verses, parallelism, and narrative setting rule over isolated letter associations.
5. **Synthesize**: one paragraph on what the word contributes to the passage''s meaning and a faithful response.

Paleo-Hebrew pictographic associations are **memory aids**, not freestanding proofs. Always submit letter insights to the grammar and context of the text.

## Worked example

Method demo: isolate one verb or noun, note the Hallelujah Scriptures rendering, then ask what the underlying Hebrew root typically conveys. Record passage, word, gloss, context, question.

## Practice

Complete these before peeking at answers.

1. What posture does “Why Word Study Matters” require?
2. Why does context outrank isolated letter associations?
3. Name one tool you may cite.

## Check your work

1. Reverent, careful, academic reading under textual control
2. Grammar and usage in the passage determine meaning
3. Teacher-approved lexicon, interlinear, or class Paleo-Hebrew chart

## Stretch

Journal one page: passage reference, key word, Paleo-Hebrew notes labeled as aids, lexicon gloss, contextual synthesis, and a concrete obedient response.

## Wrap-up

Summarize the key word(s), root insight, and contextual meaning in 4–6 sentences. Then complete the graded check below.','• Hallelujah Scriptures emphasize the Name and a return to Hebraic understanding of the text.
• Word study slows reading so meaning is not skipped; roots and usage clarify English renderings.
• We study academically and faithfully — seeking understanding for obedience, not for arguments.',1,40,'section-1','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s-KvoVzukHo');
INSERT INTO "Lesson" VALUES('cmuh9bydl09w9edan3ytxwjrw','cmuh9bydh09vtedancw8rs5y1','Paleo-Hebrew Letters: Form and Meaning Intro','Learn Paleo-Hebrew letter forms and traditional pictographic associations as study aids — with humility.','Welcome to **Bible: Hallelujah Scriptures & Paleo-Hebrew Word Study** at Prosper Preparatory (Grade 10).

