Apostrophes look small and cost big. Singular possession adds apostrophe-s. Plurals ending in s put the apostrophe after s. Irregular plurals like women take apostrophe-s.

Joint possession marks the final name once. Separate possession marks both. Pronoun possessives never take apostrophes. Expand it''s every time—if you cannot, you want its. its'' is never correct.

