INSERT INTO "Lesson" VALUES('cmuh9bz020cbzedanbo2fqgrv','cmuh9byyz0c7redandrerxelc','E4.1 Passage triage & pacing','Nine-minute passage budgets, attack order, and when to skip inside English.','# E4.1 Passage triage & pacing

## Objectives
- Budget ~9 minutes per English passage block
- Protect easy grammar points under time
- Apply now/later/guess inside a passage

## Teach
### The clock
75 questions / 45 minutes ≈ 36 seconds each; about **9 minutes** per passage block.

### Attack
Read enough local context; vertical-scan choice differences for underlined grammar; do not reread the whole essay for every rhetoric item.

### Triage
Mark sticky add/delete rationales as later; bank clean agreement/punctuation first.

### Checkpoint
After passage 2, if >~2 minutes behind, shorten rhetoric deliberation.

## Practice
1. Time a 15-item set in 9 minutes.
2. Write your personal later-trigger for rhetoric.
3. Plan bubble batches (every 5 items).





### Elite checklist
1. Read enough context—usually the full sentence, sometimes the sentence before/after for rhetoric.
2. Predict the relationship or the grammatical need before looking at choices.
3. Vertical-scan differences among the four options.
